      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Technology and globalization are not just excuses for policy shifts; they are fundamental structural drivers that often work in tandem with policy to widen the wealth gap. The \"skill-biased technological change\" allows capital and highly skilled workers to earn much more, while offshoring capital to low-wage countries has suppressed wage growth for unskilled labor. Consequently, these market forces have created a landscape where policy decisions, such as tax cuts, can now reinforce rather than correct these deepening inequalities.",
